Implemented the generation fixes and diagnostics.

- The parser now extracts Python from fenced blocks even when Gemini surrounds them with prose, and handles an opening fence without a closing one.
- Prompts now ask for one short, complete test and explicitly prohibit Markdown or incomplete code.
- If generated code has invalid syntax or lacks a `test_` function, the generator makes one repair attempt before recording failure. Refinement uses the same validation path.
- Experiment artifacts now record provider response length and finish reason, which were missing from the earlier run. That should help distinguish an incomplete model response from malformed code the model finished generating.

The artifacts show both fenced responses and code ending mid-statement, but the old run didn’t save Gemini’s finish reason, so we couldn’t determine whether those short responses were truncated. The new diagnostics should make that clear next time.

