The focused Black run completed after the fixes. All four Gemini conditions returned syntactically valid Python, and every response ended with `STOP`; none needed a syntax repair in this rerun. That confirms the updated prompt, parsing, and low-thinking configuration work for this task and repetition.

The run also exposed why the original responses were cut short: Gemini’s `max_output_tokens` includes internal thinking tokens. Google’s docs confirm that hitting this limit can produce truncated output with `MAX_TOKENS`, and recommend lowering the thinking level to leave more room for the answer ([Gemini thinking documentation](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/generate-content/thinking)). The focused run with thinking set to `low` had no `MAX_TOKENS` responses.

The one-repetition results are only a generation check, not a broad performance comparison: one-shot and retrieval produced valid tests but did not detect this Black defect; feedback and full detected it.

The rerun artifacts are in [comparison-summary.json](/E:/evidence-loop/experiments/results/low-thinking-check-rerun-20261018/comparison-summary.json), with condition details in the [Black run folder](/E:/evidence-loop/experiments/results/low-thinking-check-rerun-20261018/bugsinpy-black-021/bugsinpy-black-021-r001). Python compilation succeeded; I did not run tests.

